  "public_surface_evidence": [],
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R001",
      "instruction_quote": "- `shiv` MUST continue to support `-h`, `--help`, `--halp`, `--version`, `-e`/`--entry-point`, `-c`/`--console-script`, `-o`/`--output-file`, `-p`/`--python`, `--site-packages`, `--build-id`, `--compressed`, `--uncompressed`, `--compile-pyc`, `-E`/`--extend-pythonpath`, `--reproducible`, `--no-modify`, `--preamble`, and `--root`.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R002",
      "instruction_quote": "- `shiv-info <pyz>` MUST continue to support `-h`, `--help`, `--halp`, and `-j`/`--json`.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R003",
      "instruction_quote": "- A request that lacks both dependency-installation arguments and `--site-packages` MUST fail with status 1 and report `You must supply PIP ARGS or --site-packages!`.\n- A request that supplies input without `-o`/`--output-file` MUST fail with status 1 and report `You must provide an output file option! (--output-file/-o)`.\n- A failed dependency installation MUST fail with status 1 and report `Pip install failed!`.\n- The disallowed options `-t`, `--target`, `--editable`, `-d`, `--download`, `--user`, and `--prefix`, including applicable equals forms, MUST fail with status 1 and identify the supplied argument and its reason.\n- A Python interpreter value longer than 128 characters for the zipapp shebang MUST fail with status 1 and report `Shebang is too long, it would exceed BINPRM_BUF_SIZE! Consider /usr/bin/env`.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R004",
      "instruction_quote": "- A module entry point for the hello package MUST still print `hello world` when the archive is run. Module-entry and console-script modes MUST remain distinct.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R005",
      "instruction_quote": "- `shiv-info` text output MUST identify the archive path and its metadata. JSON output MUST be valid JSON. Both views MUST describe the same archive state, including build identifier, timestamp, interpreter, entry-point mode, compression, extraction settings, reproducibility, and recorded source hashes.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R006",
      "instruction_quote": "- Arguments not consumed by shiv MUST reach dependency installation in their original order and spelling. This includes repeated options, positional arguments, values that begin with a dash, and equals-form options. Options that shiv explicitly disallows MUST still be rejected rather than forwarded.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R007",
      "instruction_quote": "1. Use Click 8.1.7 exactly; do not retain a dependency on Click 6.7.",
      "kind": "target_postcondition"
    },
    {
      "id": "R008",
      "instruction_quote": "2. Do not remove, rename, weaken, or reinterpret existing public commands, options, supported packaging capabilities, runtime modes, error statuses, or documented diagnostics.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R009",
      "instruction_quote": "- Arguments not consumed by shiv MUST reach dependency installation in their original order and spelling. This includes repeated options, positional arguments, values that begin with a dash, and equals-form options. Options that shiv explicitly disallows MUST still be rejected rather than forwarded.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R010",
      "instruction_quote": "- A successful archive MUST be a readable, runnable zipapp with the expected bootstrap and metadata, one effective entry for each archive path, and preserved source permissions where supported. The output MUST be executable on platforms that support executable zipapps. For a newly created archive, its final POSIX mode MUST follow the established umask behavior; overwriting an archive MUST retain its existing read/write permissions while ensuring executable bits remain available.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R011",
      "instruction_quote": "- If the first extraction or build fails, no partial target or archive may remain that could be mistaken for a successful result.\n- If replacing an existing valid extraction or archive fails at any point, the complete previous result MUST remain readable and runnable, with its contents and bytes unchanged where byte identity is part of the existing behavior.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R012",
      "instruction_quote": "- A file lock MUST provide mutual exclusion across threads and processes using the same path. An already-held lock MUST block another acquisition until release.\n- A finite timeout and polling interval MUST control waiting. A timed-out acquisition MUST raise `TimeoutError` identifying the lock path, MUST not enter the protected operation, and MUST not prevent a later acquisition.",
      "kind": "preserve"
    },
    {
      "id": "R013",
      "instruction_quote": "- `shiv-info` text output MUST identify the archive path and its metadata. JSON output MUST be valid JSON. Both views MUST describe the same archive state, including build identifier, timestamp, interpreter, entry-point mode, compression, extraction settings, reproducibility, and recorded source hashes.",
      "kind": "target_postcondition"
    }
  ],
